Host shim: cc0 calls index(), which mingw's C library does not provide.

index() is the V7 spelling of strchr().  glibc still carries it and COHERENT's
own libc has it, so the target build wants the declaration as it stands;
mingw-w64 does not, and cc0 fails to link.  cc0 is the only pass that uses it.

--- a/n0/cc0.c
+++ b/n0/cc0.c
@@ -75,7 +75,7 @@
 int	s;			/* Lexical window */
 
 /* Externals. */
-extern char *index();
+#define index strchr
 extern char *getenv();
 
